        "value": "<p>Antibody Used: Anti-Inhibin monoclonal/polyclonal antibody<br>Method: IHC on formalin-fixed paraffin-embedded (FFPE) tissue<br>Controls: Positive and negative controls included</p>\n<p>Results:</p>\n<p>Parameter &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; | Description / Result<br>------------------------------------------------<br>Inhibin Positive Cells &nbsp;| [Number / Percentage] of positive cells<br>Staining Pattern &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;| [Cytoplasmic / Nuclear / Membranous]<br>Intensity of Staining &nbsp; | [Weak / Moderate / Strong]<br>Distribution &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; | [Diffuse / Focal / Patchy]<br>Background / Comments &nbsp; | [Additional remarks]</p>\n<p>Interpretation:<br>[Example:]<br>- Positive inhibin staining supports diagnosis of sex cord-stromal tumors.<br>- Negative staining argues against inhibin-expressing neoplasms.<br>- Correlate with morphology and clinical findings.</p>",
